## Notes

- Keep rows here as the loop runs; do not delete completed rows (they form an
  audit trail). The full event history lives in the append-only `log.md`.
- **Failure policy is restart-within-budget.** A `failed` row means the loop
  retries or restarts the iteration from a clean state — it does not halt.
  Increment `consecutive_fails`; reset it to 0 on the next pass. Halt only when
  `consecutive_fails` reaches N (gate G2) or the budget is hit (see
  `HUMAN-GATES.md`).
- Recover after a crash from three files: `CONTRACT.md` (what done means),
  this file (where we are), and `log.md` (what happened).
